  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2022 preprint shows early scholarly uptake: OpenAlex records 1 citation, and the reuse graph also captures 1 downstream article that reused the work. The record suggests the paper\u2019s main contribution is methodological, advancing automated assessment of rigor and transparency in scientific reporting, with publication of a peer-reviewed version under a journal DOI.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Establishing Institutional Scores With the Rigor and Transparency Index addresses a practical problem in research assessment: how to evaluate rigor and transparency at scale without relying only on manual review. The abstract frames the work as an enhancement of the Rigor and Transparency Index, designed to automatically score journals, institutions, and countries using criteria drawn from research manuscripts. That positioning aligns with the article\u2019s concept profile, which centers on transparency, checklists, and rigor, with broader relevance across medicine, psychology, computer science, and related fields.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The impact record is still early, but it is not empty. OpenAlex shows 1 citation, and the reuse graph records 1 article that has reused the work. The citing literature is concentrated in a 2026 article in Research Integrity and Peer Review, indicating that the paper is being taken up within the research integrity and evaluation space. With only a small citation base, the record supports a cautious reading: this is an emerging influence rather than a mature citation profile.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The publication trail also matters. Although the work is identified here as a preprint, the digest shows a published metric for a peer-reviewed version, suggesting that the study moved from posted content into formal journal publication. That transition strengthens the paper\u2019s credibility as a contribution to the literature on research assessment and transparency tooling.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Other signals point to limited but visible reach. The record includes OpenAIRE repository matching and a WorldCat holding, which indicate catalogued availability and discoverability, while public-discourse and event-data fields do not provide additional visible attention in this digest. Overall, the article\u2019s footprint is best described as an early-stage scholarly impact centered on reuse and method adoption in research integrity contexts.</p>",
